Define the independent unit in a sampling plan (@cm-qualification-sampling: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../../../inquiry/metrology/sources/Statistical-Handbook.lingua#r_6S3221KSX1KKGPJNXKC3N022NN", #clean-manufacturing "Choose-sample-size-for-an-explicit-information-goal.lingua#r_4XNPXHN56AKKYN1Z3T3419JWEZ") { r_58QWH01E5CR6GR9MA297KC0YH4
**Read:** [Measurement Process Characterization — NIST/SEMATECH](../../../inquiry/metrology/sources/Statistical-Handbook.lingua#r_6S3221KSX1KKGPJNXKC3N022NN), acceptance sampling and process characterization. Revisit [Sampling contributions, thresholds, and results near zero](../../../inquiry/metrology/uncertainty/Sampling-and-censoring.lingua#r_3RRJRMNNAPMVYJ9Z6VGY2DV0CG) and [Separate sampling, preparation and analysis in a comparison](../surface-measurement/Separate-sampling-preparation-and-analysis-in-a-comparison.lingua#r_45Z6TMPNGW0W9QRZ5MTMMTYACK).

The unit sampled may be a product, a location, a production run or a time interval. Ten readings from one collected sample are not ten independent samples of the manufacturing process. Preserve nesting within locations, instruments, shifts and lots.

Random selection supports an inference to a declared population. Stratification can ensure coverage of distinct operating states. Deliberate observations at likely problem locations answer targeted questions; they should not be presented as a random estimate without a model for the selection.

Samples from different days may reveal variation absent within one shift. Conversely, averaging all conditions can hide a persistent problem in one state. Decide whether the target is a mean, a high percentile, a local maximum, a rate or a fraction of unacceptable items before choosing where and when to observe.

**Work:** Design a simulated sampling plan with three locations, two operating states and repeated readings. Identify the independent units for each claim. Compare an area-weighted mean with a claim about the most vulnerable product location, retaining their different sampling requirements.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
